(7651555, 1244689, 172697, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your comments and votes :)<br/> <br/>This picture is actually part of a concept I shot in February, then finalized a couple of months ago.<br/> <br/>I''ll leave you a link below<br/><a href="//www.alessiofelicioni.net/portfolio-item/the-shape-of-nature/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.alessiofelicioni.net/portfolio-item/the-shape-of-nature/<br/></a> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=124815" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">mariuca</a> it''s beautiful how different eyes see different things, colours are the 90% of why I chose to develop this project, I''d never in a lifetime think of those pictures in B&amp;N... I mean, I''m sure they''d look good, but not for what I had in mind :) Thanks for the suggestion though, I''ll try it.<br/> <br/>Thank you everyone, <br/> <br/>Cheers<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2020-01-24 07:56:21.</i></td>', 'Thank you all for your comments and votes :) This picture is actually part of a concept I shot in February, then finalized a couple of months ago. I''ll leave you a link below//www.alessiofelicioni.net/portfolio-item/the-shape-of-nature/  mariuca it''s beautiful how different eyes see different things, colours are the 90% of why I chose to develop this project, I''d never in a lifetime think of those pictures in B&N... I mean, I''m sure they''d look good, but not for what I had in mind :) Thanks for the suggestion though, I''ll try it. Thank you everyone,  Cheers', '2020-01-24 07:55:54.000000', '2020-01-24 07:56:21.000000', 0),
(7651558, 1244377, 173844, '<td valign="top">Truffaut was here.  Ran out of time before I could comment on this wistful, thoughtful, winning image.  Feels like the immensity of time in childhood, the taking in of the world.  The tower may not be straight, but she or he is.</td>', 'Truffaut was here.  Ran out of time before I could comment on this wistful, thoughtful, winning image.  Feels like the immensity of time in childhood, the taking in of the world.  The tower may not be straight, but she or he is.', '2020-01-24 08:47:36.000000', NULL, 0),
